WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
Welcome back. Today we finally get to attention.

00:06.000 --> 00:13.000
Our bigram model only ever looked at the single previous token to predict the next one.

00:13.000 --> 00:20.000
That throws away everything earlier in the context, which is a lot of information.

00:20.000 --> 00:27.000
Self-attention lets every token look back at all the earlier tokens and decide how much each one matters.

00:27.000 --> 00:34.000
We compute the weights as a softmax of queries dotted with keys, scaled by one over the square root of the head size.

00:34.000 --> 00:40.000
The scaling keeps the softmax from saturating when the head size gets large.

00:40.000 --> 00:47.000
In code, we multiply q by k transposed and scale it, then mask out the future with the lower triangular matrix.

00:47.000 --> 00:54.000
Filling the masked positions with minus infinity makes their softmax weight exactly zero.

00:54.000 --> 01:00.000
Then the softmax over the last dimension gives each row weights that sum to one.
